\f0\fs24 \cf0 AetherReader\
\
Description:\
A web-based ereader that connects to various cloud storage solutions, allowing users to read their books on any device with a web browser.\
\
Functional Requirements:\
The app should allow for the creation of user accounts\
The app should not store any personal information of the user other than a name (prefer passkeys, we don\'92t want to store passwords)\
The app should allow users to connect a folder/location in either Google Drive, Dropbox, or Nextcloud in order to have their books available in the app\
The app should support all common ebook formats (epub, mobi, pdf, etc.)\
The app should keep track of the reading progress for the user and allow for quickly resuming reading on multiple devices\
The app should have a native dark mode and allow the user to switch between light and dark mode\
\
Technical preferences:\
The app should use Python and Flask in the back end\
The app should use a well-know, easy to maintain/update framework for the front end\
The app should be coded such that I can easily follow the backend and frontend logic because I want to be able to maintain it myself after the initial devlopment\
I already have a github repo to use for this project (https://github.com/benhowlett/AetherReader.git)\
I will be hosting this on a linode VPS, which I already have set up and I have the url aetherreader.com pointed to it}